# Security Policy

## Supported versions

Only the latest version on the `main` branch receives fixes.

| Version | Supported |
| ------- | --------- |
| `main` (latest) | ✅ |
| Older commits / forks | ❌ |

## Reporting a vulnerability

**Please do not open a public issue for security problems.**

Report privately using GitHub's [private vulnerability reporting](https://github.com/zhiggera/solar-lunar-dial/security/advisories/new) (Security tab → "Report a vulnerability").

Please include:

- A description of the issue and its potential impact
- Steps to reproduce
- Browser / Windows version, if relevant

You can expect an initial response within 7 days. Once confirmed, a fix will be prioritized and you'll be credited in the release notes unless you prefer otherwise.

## What the Windows .exe builders do

The "Build Windows 11 .EXE" options generate scripts that run on your computer. You should always review a script before running it. Here's exactly what they do:

**Option 1 (`Install-SolarLunarWidget.bat`) and Option 2 (PowerShell command):**

1. Run PowerShell with `-ExecutionPolicy Bypass` for that session only (no system settings are changed).
2. Stop any running `SolarLunarWidget.exe` process.
3. Create `%LOCALAPPDATA%\SolarLunarWidget\` and write the widget HTML there.
4. Download the official `Microsoft.Web.WebView2` package from `nuget.org` (first run only).
5. Generate an icon and compile a small C# program using the .NET Framework compiler (`csc.exe`) that ships with Windows.
6. Copy `SolarLunarWidget.exe` to your Desktop and launch it.

No administrator rights are requested, nothing is installed system-wide, and no registry keys are written.

**Option 3 (Electron builder):** requires Node.js and runs `npm install electron @electron/packager`, then packages an `.exe` into a folder on your Desktop.

**To uninstall:** close the widget from its tray icon, then delete `%LOCALAPPDATA%\SolarLunarWidget\` (or `SolarLunarOverlay\`) and the `.exe` on your Desktop.

Because the compiled `.exe` is unsigned, Windows SmartScreen or antivirus software may warn about it. This is expected for unsigned, locally compiled programs.

## Privacy and network requests

The widget makes these requests at runtime:

| Service | Data sent | Purpose |
| ------- | --------- | ------- |
| Open-Meteo | Latitude/longitude, date | Weather |
| Nominatim (OpenStreetMap) | Your city search text | Geocoding |
| Browser geolocation | Only if you click the GPS icon | Your coordinates |
| cdn.tailwindcss.com, cdnjs, Google Fonts | Standard page requests | Styling, SunCalc, fonts |

Settings (location, layout, opacity) are saved only in your browser's `localStorage`. Nothing is sent to the author.

## Scope

In scope: the code in this repository, including the generated builder scripts.

Out of scope: vulnerabilities in third-party services or libraries listed above (please report those to their maintainers).
